":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","number":16,"title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5791,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T22:40:26Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-08-19T14:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:19:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122598.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10969\r\n- Works toward adding runtime checks for Callable-Signal upon connecting (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14266 for more info)\r\n  Please note this's not best solution, as we could statically check, which'll be better, but adding runtime checks is better then having no checks at all.\r\n\r\n<details><summary><h2>Interested for a spin? (Testing changes out)</h2></summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you're a user of the Engine, or experienced with code base, you can test these changes by:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n\r\n<li>Downloading the CI builds (<a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307324266\">Windows</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307996104\">MacOS</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11308305862\">Linux</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/37212232316/artifacts/11307930326\">Android</a>)\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li>having any <code>Callable</code> in your script, and calling <code>.get_method_info()</code>, which returns a Dictionary representing the method (see <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.h#L48\">struct def</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.cpp#L37-L51\">Dictionary convertion</a> for more info). returned Dictionary contains following keys:\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><code>name</code>: name of method (of type <code>String</code>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>args</code>: an array of dictionaries, each one represents an argument (which's a Dictionary representing <b>PropertyInfo type</b>, see below)</li>\r\n    <li><code>default_args</code>: an array of variants representing default values of optional arguments.</li>\r\n    <li><code>flags</code>: a integer representing what the method is (see <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/method_info.h#L36\">MethodFlags enum</a>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>id</code>: unique identifier (of type <code>int</code>)</li>\r\n    <li><code>return</code>: what the method returns (Dictionary representing <b>PropertyInfo type</b>, see below)</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<b>PropertyInfo as Dictionary:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><code>name</code>: name of the argument, which's a <code>String</code></li>\r\n<li><code>class_name</code>: name of argument's class, which's a <code>StringName</code></li>\r\n<li><code>type</code>: type of argument, which's a <code>Variant::Type</code>, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/94a23991c683254d8b5ef63f4f5e017b995c4c2f/core/variant/variant.h#L97\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n<li><code>hint</code>: a hint useful to know what this argument is, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/property_info.h#L39\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n<li><code>hint_string</code>: string representation of <code>hint</code></li>\r\n<li><code>usage</code>: a useful hint on what to do with this argument, as an <code>int</code> (Enum value), <a href=\"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3088fecf1837aa22fcf2bccae413598a2e91766/core/object/property_info.h#L88\">enum definition here</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details><summary><h2>Use of AI</h2></summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<p>I've used AI only in specific instances, of which are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>better understand C#/GD script interop, as somethings weren't clear to me, this allowed me to test implement of <code>get_method_info()</code> in <code>ManagedCallable</code>, it didn't tell straight away on how to trigger it, used my knowledge from reading godot docs about C#/GD Interop and asked it to write a simple example, which I've read through and changed a lot to fit my needs.</br>\r\nAI model used was Google's Gemini AI, specific model version is unknown to me, as I've asked it few weeks ago, and I'm unfamiliar with AI as a whole.. so idk how to extract model number.. apologies for my ignorance 😓</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n</details>","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122598/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}